 "title": "Blob storage",
 "short": "Keep big files by key, and only the key in your database.",
 "what": "Photos, videos and backups are big blobs of bytes that you never search inside. Blob storage (object storage, like S3) keeps each file under a key, copies it to several disks, and serves it over HTTP. Your database keeps only the key and a few details.",
