 "python": "import hashlib\nblobs = {}       # blob store: key -> bytes\nposts = {}       # database: post id -> small row\n\nphoto = bytes(4_000_000)                           # a 4 MB photo\nkey = \"photos/u7/\" + hashlib.md5(photo).hexdigest()[:8] + \".jpg\"\nblobs[key] = photo                                 # the phone uploads here directly\nposts[88] = {\"user\": 7, \"key\": key, \"size\": len(photo)}\n\nprint(posts[88])\nprint(\"db row ~\", len(str(posts[88])), \"bytes, blob\", len(blobs[key]), \"bytes\")\nprint(\"1M photos a day:\", 1_000_000 * len(photo) // 10**12, \"TB a day\")",
 "output": "{'user': 7, 'key': 'photos/u7/90b741f9.jpg', 'size': 4000000}\ndb row ~ 61 bytes, blob 4000000 bytes\n1M photos a day: 4 TB a day",
